    "faq": [
        {
            "a": "Partly. 12 of the 16 versions of Z.ai GLM in the OpenRouter catalog publish open weights, and 4 are served over APIs only. The family's repositories on Hugging Face declare the MIT licence, and some carry a custom licence set out on the model card.",
            "q": "Is Z.ai GLM open source?"
        },
        {
            "a": "Through the OpenRouter catalog, Z.ai GLM costs from $0.06 to $2.8 per million input tokens and from $0.4 to $12 per million output tokens, depending on the version. The cheapest is GLM 4.7 Flash.",
            "q": "How much does Z.ai GLM cost?"
        },
        {
            "a": "GLM 5.3 Prime is the newest version in the OpenRouter catalog, added on 2026-09-23.",
            "q": "What is the newest Z.ai GLM model?"
        },
        {
            "a": "Z.ai GLM versions accept image, text and video as input and produce text. All 16 versions support reasoning, and context windows run from 65,536 to 1,048,576 tokens.",
            "q": "What can Z.ai GLM do?"
        },
        {
            "a": "Z.ai GLM is developed by Zhipu AI. Zhipu AI is a company headquartered in Beijing.",
            "q": "Who makes Z.ai GLM?"
        },
        {
            "a": "In the OpenRouter catalog, 42 providers serve it.",
            "q": "Where can I use Z.ai GLM?"
